      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's the \"move fast and break things\" culture. they took our core work, stripped the stability safeguards to make it more \"efficient\" for standard hardware, and then rebranded the whole thing. i remember the day the NDA was finalized—it felt like watching a crime scene being cleaned up. if someone were to actually try and reconstruct the original intended stability protocols from the 2017 documentation we had, do you think the current architectures would even be able to converge?",
